{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful ruler who reigned from 1145 to 1199. He was a prominent figure in the Crusader states particularly in Tripoli. His reign marked a period of significant expansion and consolidation of Tripoli's territory and influence. Raymond III inherited the countship at a young age and quickly established himself as a capable and ambitious leader.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension*\n\nRaymond was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli. His early life was focused on military training and political maneuvering. He proved to be a skilled warrior and diplomat. His ascent to the countship was relatively swift following his father's death in 1145. Raymond immediately began to assert his authority and expand Tripoli's control over surrounding regions. He skillfully navigated the complex political landscape of the Crusader states forging alliances and resolving conflicts. He focused on strengthening Tripoli's defenses and fostering economic growth.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Territorial Expansion*\n\nRaymond III's reign was characterized by numerous military campaigns. He successfully defended Tripoli against various attacks from Muslim forces and other Crusader rivals. He expanded Tripoli's territory through conquest and strategic alliances. He asserted control over coastal regions and established fortified settlements. His military prowess and strategic thinking earned him respect and solidified Tripoli's position as a major power in the Levant. He also engaged in campaigns against the Seljuk Turks demonstrating Tripoli's strength and resolve. Raymond's military victories helped to secure Tripoli's borders and protect its interests.\n\n*Political and Economic Policies*\n\nRaymond III implemented several important political and economic policies. He reformed the administration of Tripoli making it more efficient and effective. He promoted trade and commerce fostering economic growth and prosperity. He encouraged the development of agriculture and industry. He also strengthened the relationship between Tripoli and the Latin kingdoms of Europe. Raymond's policies contributed to the stability and prosperity of Tripoli during his reign. He fostered a sense of unity and identity among the people of Tripoli. His efforts to improve the lives of his subjects helped to solidify his popularity and maintain his power. He invested in infrastructure improving roads and ports benefiting both the economy and the military.\n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli left a lasting legacy as a strong and effective ruler. His reign was a period of significant growth and prosperity for Tripoli. He successfully defended the countship against numerous threats and expanded its territory and influence. His policies contributed to the stability and prosperity of the region. He is remembered as one of the most successful and influential counts of Tripoli. His impact on the history of the Crusader states and the Levant remains significant.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1804991215467453}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -6.115249561844394e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.08474750816822052}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.03216259181499481}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5741356611251831}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.6246256232261658}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.6148910522460938}, {"token": "▁reigned", "logprob": -0.5363537669181824}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -1.0648558139801025}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.001955979270860553}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00012170527770649642}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0012034086976200342}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -0.7125585675239563}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -2.3375866413116455}, {"token": "▁to", "log